build/bin
node_modules
frontend/dist

# Wails: the generated bindings are produced at build time from the Go source,
# and are not committed -- the same rule GoPCA Desktop follows. They were
# tracked here until #886, which is how three of the six files came to be
# committed with mode 755 and the other three with 644 without anyone
# noticing: checked-in generated code drifts quietly, because nothing compares
# it against what generates it.
#
# Anchor the pattern with a leading slash. An unanchored `bindings/` matches a
# directory of that name at any depth, which would also swallow any
# src/__mocks__/bindings test doubles added later -- exactly the trap GoPCA
# Desktop's .gitignore had.
/frontend/bindings/

# Wails v3 build system
.task/
*.syso
build/linux/appimage/build/
